# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers
# https://opennext.js.org/cloudflare/caching#static-assets-caching
#
# Content-hashed build output: a file's name changes whenever its content does, so a browser may keep
# it for a year without asking again. Measured 2026-09-14: every script here was served with
# "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate", so each repeat visit re-asked the server about every chunk --
# one round trip per file, on whatever connection a guest has at the venue.
#
# Nothing else in public/ is content-hashed. Fonts, logos and backgrounds keep their names when they
# are replaced, so nothing else may be marked immutable: tests/static-headers.test.ts holds that line.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=31536000,immutable
